<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Honda Tadamasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1575">1575</a>–<a href="/years/1631">1631</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Honda Tadamasa was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a>, eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honda-tadakatsu">Honda Tadakatsu</a>, who succeeded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuwana">Kuwana</a> and in 1617 was moved to the Himeji domain. His son married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senhime">Senhime</a>, granddaughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>, tying the family closely to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>. At Himeji he extended the castle's western enclosure.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/honda-tadamasa.jpg" alt="Honda Tadamasa" width="320" height="620" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%9C%AC%E5%A4%9A%E5%BF%A0%E6%94%BF.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
